  "backstory": "Torvin is a hardened soldier, wearied by years of service in the king's army. He has seen the brutality of war firsthand, and although he carries the scars of battle, both physical and emotional, he remains steadfast. He left the army seeking a quieter life, but his ingrained sense of duty and his combat skills often draw him back into conflict.",
  "flaws": [
    "Haunted by nightmares of past battles.",
    "Prone to fits of anger when reminded of his military service.",
    "Distrustful of authority."
  ],
  "ideals": [
    "Discipline. The most important thing is doing your duty. (Lawful)",
    "Responsibility. I do what I must and obey just authority. (Lawful)",
    "Greater Good. My gifts are meant to alleviate the suffering of others. (Good)"
  ],
  "bonds": [
    "I would still lay down my life for the people I served with.",
    "I am trying to atone for a terrible decision I made during the war."
  ],
  "traits": [
    "I'm always polite and respectful.",
    "I am haunted by memories of war. I can't get the images of violence out of my mind.",
    "I face problems head-on. A simple, direct solution is the best path to success."
  ],
